    "changes": [],
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a> </i></p><p><b>Emplacement Points:</b>&nbsp;1</p><p><b>Size Restriction:&nbsp;</b> Colossal or Larger</p><p>Fuel Converters transform matter into usable <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fuel\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fuel\">Fuel</a> that can keep a starship running even over long journeys. While Fuel Converters never eliminate the need to refuel during visits to spaceports, they can extend the amount of time between visits and reduce <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fuel\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fuel\">Fuel</a> costs. Fuel Converters come in a variety of forms, including solid fuel converters, gas scoops, and solar converters. If the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot_(Vehicle_Combat)\" title=\"Pilot (Vehicle Combat)\">Pilot</a> of a Starship with Fuel Converters spends at least 1 hour gathering <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fuel\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fuel\">Fuel</a> in realspace, the ship regains one unit of fuel&nbsp;(enough for one day's travel in realspace, one hour's travel in atmosphere or in combat, or one Hyperspace jump).</p>",
    "cost": "2400 (Base)",
